% Approved notes UI integration: web/notes.js, web/notes.css, existing app.js/index.html.
% Direct implementation; future PDD synchronization has not run.

Add Notes & solutions navigation to the existing Reading Room. Book cards and
selected reader sections link to matching topics. Render master and all three
companions with portrait PDF, screen PDF and source links. Topic cards expose
derivation, legacy references, Sage code, numerical code and evidence. Search
topic/manuscript text and support book/section filters and a return-to-book link.

Consume GET /api/notes; source/PDF downloads use registered /note-asset/<id>.
Render untrusted strings as escaped text. Do not execute downloaded sources.
Use existing navigation/save protection so drafts survive failed/conflicting
saves before following internal notes links. No browser CDN, telemetry or
remote model dependency. Notes remain usable when book bundles are missing.

MUST NOT turn visiting a derivation or seeing a passing check into completion
of a personal reading/derivation/implementation checkbox. Explain stale or
absent evidence and missing optional assets without displaying verified badges.
Maintain responsive layouts with no horizontal overflow at 390px width.

Evidence: tests/browser.cjs exercises original reading persistence plus topic
search, asset access, book/derivation round trips and mobile layout; reject
unexpected external requests and browser errors.
